{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310597,"nonce":"1QvFkuAZy7/94ShcfJzU4TlMcP0=","title":"FIXED 2026-06-30 — enum through Map\u003cK,Enum\u003e got int-boxed on the var-binding path → corrupt variant tag (was nue's silent GGUF-load crash). ...","message":"The narrowing below (\"mixed payload / 13 variants / Bool+Str+Arr names\") was a RED HERRING. Real trigger = **`var v = map.get(k); switch(v)` (var-binding) FAILS; `switch(map.get(k))` (inline) always worked** + cross-module dispatch. VERIFIED: /tmp/orpat3.hx single+orpat=2048, /tmp/xmod metaInt=2048 (was SIGILL 132), native suite 156/156 byte-identical, q4km/simd16i8_bitops/simd4i32 PASS. Fixes (all uncommitted, in compiler/src):\n1. **ast_lowering.rs `compute_type_substitution` Class arm (~13492):** `Map\u003cString,MetaValue\u003e.get` is @:multiType-resolved to `Class{StringMap,[MetaValue]}` (single arg); `get_class_type_params(StringMap)`→None (StringMap `\u003cT\u003e` lowered in a different ast_lowering instance) → bailed `NoChange(Null\u003cV\u003e)` → abstract. FIX = positional fallback: params-empty + non-empty type_args + bare/Optional-wrapped TypeParameter return → substitute against the LAST type_arg → concrete `Optional\u003cMetaValue\u003e`.\n2. **hir_to_mir.rs `maybe_box_for_optional` (~23788) + new `optional_inner_is_boxable_primitive`:** boxing decided on IR type; an enum lowers to `IrType::I64` which matched the box-primitive set → enum int-boxed via `haxe_box_int_ptr` before the switch → wrong tag → -1. FIX = gate on TAST kind: only Int/Float/Bool/Char (through abstracts) box; enums/classes/refs/Usize/Ptr/SIMD skipped (already nullable ptrs). Null\u003cInt\u003e-via-generic still boxes (safe).\n3. **ast_lowering.rs `lower_type` Class + TypeAlias arms (~5911) + `new Map()` hint fallback (~8141):** CROSS-MODULE — user file lowers before haxe/ds/Map.hx, so `Map` is a stale `SymbolKind::Class` placeholder; lower_type's Class arm had NO @:multiType resolution → field kept abstract `Map` → `.get/.set` dispatched to default IMap impl `haxe.ds.BalancedTree` → fails to monomorphize cross-module → trap stub → SIGILL. FIX = resolve `Map\u003cK,V\u003e`→concrete container in Class+TypeAlias arms too.\nDiagnostic gotcha that cost ~5 runs: `rayzor run` caches stale imported modules — ALWAYS `--no-cache` when editing them. Obsolete narrowing notes kept below for history.\n\n**CORRECTION 2026-07-01: this fix did NOT unblock nue.** nue's native GGUF-load crash is a SEPARATE bug — `metaInt`'s or-pattern match emits `haxe_unbox_int_ptr` on a RAW Int enum payload → derefs it → SIGSEGV. See [[bugs_nue_metaint_unbox_raw_enum_payload]]. This enum-Map fix is real (fixed orpat3 wrong-value + xmod SIGILL) but was a RED HERRING for nue.\n\nORIGINAL (now-obsolete) ROOT-CAUSE notes: nue's native llama-chat \"silent crash during GGUF load\" (Main.hx blamed tensorsFromReader — WRONG). Real site: `metadataFromReader` → `reader.metaInt(\"llama.embedding_length\")` SIGSEGVs reading a `MetaValue` enum out of `Map\u003cString,MetaValue\u003e` (`findMeta`=`meta.get`). `metaString` survives because Str is one variant; `metaInt`'s value (U32) comes back corrupt.\n\nTHE COMPILER BUG (minimal repro **/tmp/orpat3.hx**, native cranelift, DETERMINISTIC): an enum value stored in `Map\u003cK,Enum\u003e` and retrieved via `.get()` comes back with a CORRUPTED VARIANT TAG. `case U32(x)` then doesn't match (→ `case _` → -1); an or-pattern matches the wrong arm and extracts a truncated POINTER as the Int (e.g. -1013077008). DIRECT (non-Map) values match fine. The enum is stored in the map as a raw `u64` pointer to a `{tag@0:i32, payload@8:i64}` heap struct (alloc 16); `single()` reads tag@0==4; after Map round-trip tag@0 != 4.\n\nNARROWING (~15 runs, all DETERMINISTIC — do NOT re-derive): the bug needs the FULL `MetaValue` shape; every reduction PASSES:\n- pure-Int enum (even 13 var) via Map: OK. Int+Float only: OK. Int+Bool/Str/Arr (no Float): OK. Int+Float+Str (3 var): OK. 2-field variant (Arr(a,b)): OK. ENoFloat+1Float: OK.\n- A structurally-IDENTICAL clone of MetaValue with RENAMED variants (N0..N7,NF1,NF2,NBool,NStr,NArr): **PASSES**. The actual MetaValue names (U8..I64,F32,F64,**Bool,Str,Arr**): **FAILS**.\n- Renaming variants ONE at a time back to Bool / Str / Arr each PASSES; renaming ALL THREE (Bool+Str+Arr together, = real MetaValue) FAILS. So the trigger is the COMBINATION of variant names `Bool`+`Str`+`Arr` in the full enum — renaming LATER variants (idx 10-12) corrupts an EARLIER variant's (U32, idx 4) Map round-trip.\nTWO ANGLES CONFIRMED (darmie's prompt — both were the right call):\n1. **CROSS-MODULE AMPLIFIES IT.** Same-module repro (orpat3, enum+Map+match all in Main) only returns a WRONG VALUE (-1) and runs to completion. The CROSS-MODULE repro /tmp/xmod (enum `MetaValue` + `Map\u003cString,MetaValue\u003e` + `metaInt` in module `Reader`, called from `Main` — EXACTLY nue GGUFReader's structure) **SIGILLs (exit 132), no output** — matching nue's hard crash. So cross-module turns wrong-value into a hard crash (corrupt tag → bad jump-table target). Repro needs a rayzor.toml with class-paths=[\".\"].\n2. **IT IS A MISSING/WRONG UNBOX (the typetag).** `metaInt`'s MIR reads the variant tag straight from `map.get`'s result (`load i32 @ offset 0`) with NO `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr`. The value is BOXED as a `DynamicValue {type_id@0, value_ptr}`, so reading offset 0 yields the **type_id, not the variant tag** → switch never matches (→ `_`/-1 same-module; → garbage jump → SIGILL cross-module). The compiler emitted the match against the RAW enum layout but the Map handed back a BOXED value (or boxed with a wrong/zero type_id). LEADING FIX AREA: the Map\u003cK,enum\u003e get-side must unbox (haxe_unbox_reference_ptr) before the match, OR the box/type_id must be consistent — this is the known \"box tags w/ TAST id, runtime uses deterministic header id\" consistency work ([[bugs_cross_module_dynamic_object_reflection]], [[bugs_import_xmodule_member_resolution]]). The shape-dependence (orpat3 boxes, orpat12 doesn't) = the monomorphizer decides box-vs-raw per enum shape; the get-side match assumes raw. NOT YET FIXED but now LOCALIZED to the box/unbox-consistency path, not \"deep enum representation\".\n\nDIAGNOSTIC GOTCHAS (cost ~5 wasted runs):\n1. **`rayzor run` MIR cache serves STALE imported (non-entry) modules** — editing GGUFLoader/GGUFReader and re-running showed none of the new traces + masked the SIGSEGV as a clean exit 1. ALWAYS `--no-cache` when editing imported modules; with it the real exit was 139 (SIGSEGV).\n2. **`Sys.println` (stdout) block-buffers when redirected → lost on hard crash**; `trace()` (stderr) survives.\n\nSTATUS: Phase 4 (pure-Haxe Q4 matmul in Linear.forward, gated RAYZOR_HAXE_MATMUL — Q4Matmul.hx) is kernel-validated; e2e blocked by THIS bug. Uncommitted debug traces remain in GGUFLoader.hx + GGUFReader.hx (gated RAYZOR_DBG_LOAD) — remove before committing. Repros: /tmp/orpat3.hx (fail) vs /tmp/orpat12.hx (pass). See [[perf_haxe_qmatmul_blocked_on_simd_inlining]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_enum_mixed_payload_map_corruption` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}